---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const setup = `git clone https://github.com/mdbase-dev/mdbase-connect.git
cd mdbase-connect
corepack enable
pnpm install
pnpm build`;

const download = `curl -fsSLo packages/devkit/sandbox-quickstart.mjs \\
  https://mdbase.dev/examples/sandbox-quickstart.mjs

node packages/devkit/sandbox-quickstart.mjs`;

const example = `import { unwrapOperation } from "@mdbase-dev/connect";
import { createSandbox } from "@mdbase-dev/connect-dev";

const { client, transport } = createSandbox({
  records: [{
    path: "tasks/first.md",
    types: ["task"],
    frontmatter: {
      type: "task",
      title: "Read the collection",
      completed: false
    }
  }]
});

const first = unwrapOperation(
  await client.read({ path: "tasks/first.md" })
);

const created = unwrapOperation(await client.create({
  type: "task",
  path: "tasks/second.md",
  frontmatter: {
    type: "task",
    title: "Update one record",
    completed: false
  }
}));

const updated = unwrapOperation(await client.update({
  path: created.path,
  patch: { completed: true },
  if_revision: created.revision
}));

const tasks = unwrapOperation(await client.query({
  types: ["task"],
  limit: 20
}));

console.log(\`Read: \${first.frontmatter.title}\`);
console.log(
  \`Updated: \${updated.path} (completed: \${updated.frontmatter.completed})\`
);
console.log(\`Task records: \${tasks.results.length}\`);
console.log(
  \`Markdown paths: \${transport.snapshot()
    .map((record) => record.path)
    .join(", ")}\`
);`;

const output = `Read: Read the collection
Updated: tasks/second.md (completed: true)
Task records: 2
Markdown paths: tasks/first.md, tasks/second.md`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Run the source-built SDK sandbox"
  description="Build the current beta packages from source, then run typed operations against an in-memory collection with no account or service."
  active="quickstart"
  headings={[
    { href: "#prerequisites", label: "Prerequisites" },
    { href: "#build", label: "1. Build the packages" },
    { href: "#run", label: "2. Run the example" },
    { href: "#read", label: "3. Read the code" },
    { href: "#result", label: "4. Check the result" },
    { href: "#next", label: "5. Continue" }
  ]}
>
  <div class="callout callout--success">
    <strong>Local sandbox · source build · no account required</strong>
    <p>
      This example uses the real typed collection client and the deterministic
      developer sandbox. It keeps every record in memory and makes no network
      requests.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="prerequisites">Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Git;</li>
    <li>Node 24 LTS;</li>
    <li>Corepack, which installs the repository's pinned pnpm version.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="build">1. Build the current packages</h2>
  <p>
    The Connect packages await their first npm publication. Build the exact
    beta packages from the public repository for this example.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={setup} language="sh" label="Terminal" />

  <h2 id="run">2. Download and run the complete example</h2>
  <p>
    Save the example inside the developer package so Node resolves the local
    workspace packages. The final command prints the result and exits.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={download} language="sh" label="Terminal" />
  <p>
    You can also
    {" "}<a href="/examples/sandbox-quickstart.mjs" download>download the example file</a>
    {" "}and save it as
    {" "}<code>packages/devkit/sandbox-quickstart.mjs</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="read">3. See what the example does</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={example} language="js" label="packages/devkit/sandbox-quickstart.mjs" />
  <p>
    <code>createSandbox()</code> returns the same
    {" "}<code>MdbaseCollectionClient</code> boundary used by a connected
    collection. The example reads one seed record, creates a second record,
    updates it with its revision token, and queries both task records.
  </p>

  <h2 id="result">4. Check the expected result</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={output} language="text" label="Expected output" />
  <p>
    A stale revision fails with a
    {" "}<code>concurrent_modification</code> diagnostic. The sandbox also supports
    typed CRUD, pagination, read defaults, and change cursors. CEL expressions,
    authorization, routing, and filesystem behavior belong in real-stack
    integration tests.
  </p>

  <h2 id="next">5. Continue to a real collection</h2>
  <p>
    The next guide adds an application manifest, a provisionable workout
    contract, browser authorization, and one approved local or hosted
    collection.
  </p>
  <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
    <a class="button button--primary" href="/sdk/connect-quickstart/">
      Connect a browser application
    </a>
    <a class="button" href="/sdk/testing/">Understand the test boundary</a>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
